{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_000161","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"A multimodal predictive framework uses clinical, imaging, genomic, and environmental data, but the abstract does not describe a substantive text or language-model component. This fits a non-text biomedical model paper.","evidence_snippet":"integrates structured clinical records, radiological imaging features, genomic mutation profiles and environmental exposure variables"},{"record_id":"rec_000162","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract explicitly frames the work as a lecture-style tutorial surveying methods and foundation models rather than presenting a primary model. It discusses spatial omics and histopathology methods, not a new text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"This lecture-style tutorial surveys the algorithmic foundations and recent advances"},{"record_id":"rec_000163","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"NeuroOmics-Net is a multimodal biomedical deep learning framework over MRI, EEG, and gene expression, but the abstract does not indicate a substantive text or language component. It is therefore outside the text-bio scope.","evidence_snippet":"integrates structural magnetic resonance imaging (sMRI), electroencephalography (EEG), and gene expression data"},{"record_id":"rec_000164","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes masked-language-model fine-tuning of genomic transformers on ancient DNA reconstruction, which is a clear sequence-language modeling setup. The bridge between token modeling and biological sequence reconstruction is substantive.","evidence_snippet":"standard masked-language-model fine-tuning ... apply it to ancient DNA reconstruction ... DNABERT-2 runs"},{"record_id":"rec_000165","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is centered on releasing the Dayhoff Atlas datasets and associated protein language models, making it primarily a resource/dataset paper. Although it includes generative protein models, the abstract foregrounds the atlas and data release.","evidence_snippet":"presenting the Dayhoff Atlas of protein sequence data and generative models ... release the Dayhoff Atlas code, datasets, and models"},{"record_id":"rec_000166","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"PACMOS is an R package for projecting samples into pretrained MOFA latent spaces and classifying them, which is a tooling/application layer around an existing method. The abstract does not describe a substantive text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"an R package that provides a generalizable approach to project query samples into pretrained MOFA latent factor spaces"},{"record_id":"rec_000167","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The paper studies genomic language models and uses sparse dictionary learning plus causal intervention to validate features inside them. That is a substantive sequence-language modeling paper with a clear biological bridge.","evidence_snippet":"genomic language models ... Top-k sparse autoencoders ... causally used to represent cell-type-specific TF binding"},{"record_id":"rec_000168","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract states that GROVER, a DNA language model, is fine-tuned for replication timing and then combined with epigenetic data in a multimodal model. This supports both a text-like sequence component and a substantive bio bridge.","evidence_snippet":"GROVER (Genome Rules Obtained Via Extracted Representations), a DNA language model, trained purely on DNA sequence can be fine-tuned for RT"}]}
